 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No cup, no wine, no water, no body drawn. Footsteps for «عابري سبيل» (both tafsirs: passing through the mosque), geometric for «عفوا غفورا», two paths for «أن تضلوا السبيل». 43:9-12 carries Al-Muyassar's note (shared by As-Sa'di: «منسوخة بتحريم الخمر مطلقا») that this came before wine was forbidden outright. 43:20-22 (illness: the tafsirs word the condition differently) and 43:26-37 are not glossed. STAGING v4: 43: a desert with a camel; nobody is on screen while intoxication, major impurity, illness, the privy or touching women are recited (43:1-34): only the camera, a gust on the journey (43:25) and the footsteps plate. A traveller appears on 43:35 (no water found), walks in, sits on 43:38 (dry ablution with clean earth, camera on the ground), stands and prays (ruku, sujud) as the verse closes. No cup, no water, no body drawn. 44: the People of the Book (Al-Muyassar: the Jews given part of the Torah) in a town at dusk: book plate on 44:8, they turn away on 44:9 (preferring error), speak and point at the believers on 44:11-13 (wishing them to stray, two paths plate); the believers are not shown straying; the Prophet is not shown."
 },
